16254 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Our Royal Cinnamon comes from the mountains of Quang Nam in central Vietnam\056 This\narea was historically famous for spicy\054 sweet cinnamon\054 but in the last decade\054 the\ncommodity market has shifted further north\054 where the prices are lower\056 Everyone told\nus that this area wasn\047t worth visiting and that their heirloom cinnamon variety wasn\047t\nbeing harvested anymore\056 We were very happy to discover that\047s not the case \055 the\ncinnamon here IS being harvested\054 and is incredible\054 probably the most intense we\047ve\never tasted\056)
     /K [ 3526 ]
     /P 16255 0 R
     /Pg 9212 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

16255 0 obj
  << /K [ 16254 0 R ]
     /P 18492 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 9212 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

16256 0 obj
  << /ActualText (They use a technique for harvesting cinnamon that we\047ve never encountered before \055\ninstead of chopping down the tree to harvest the bark\054 they make a deep cut around\nthe base of the tree and let the bark dry on the tree for a couple of weeks before\nharvesting it\056 That makes it easier to harvest\054 but it also concentrates essential oils\nrather than letting them evaporate as the bark dries in the hot sun\056 The bark comes off\nthe tree mostly dry and very intensely spicy and sweet\054 with a beautiful fragrance that\nwe could smell from half a mile away\056)
     /K [ 3527 ]
     /P 16257 0 R
     /Pg 9212 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

